{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Your gear.</b> The pouch — one hangs it on the belt around the waist." "<b>And hunt game for me.</b> And if you ask: how could the matter succeed for him if he ate forbidden food unwittingly — now, if even the livestock of the righteous etc.? One may answer: he did not eat from his slaughter since he was a heretic, and the matter is known, for he prefaced him with goat skins; and what it writes 'for game in his mouth,' that is before he apostatized." "<b>Game.</b> The extra hei warns him of five things: shehiyah (delay), derasah (pressing), chaladah (covering), hagramah (deflection), ikkur (uprooting) — which invalidate the slaughter."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:12.858472856Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}